From: airoha-port <airoha@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: airoha: attach the external PHY based on dev->phydev

phylink_of_phy_connect() returns 0 without attaching a PHY when the link mode
is MLO_AN_FIXED, and a close/reopen cycle clears netdev->phydev.  The
"connect once" flag therefore ended up set while netdev->phydev stayed NULL on
the 2.5G port (ethtool showed only "Link detected: no", the PHY read_status was
never polled, copper never linked).  Guard on dev->phydev instead.

Signed-off-by: airoha-port <airoha@local>
---
diff -ruN a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-11 11:22:18.385277301 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c	2026-10-11 11:22:18.389277397 +0800
@@ -1920,7 +1920,15 @@
 		 * with a "Led ... renamed ... due to name collision" message
 		 * confirming the second attach.
 		 */
-		if (!port->phy_connected) {
+		/* Decide on dev->phydev, not on a "we connected once" flag:
+		 * phylink_of_phy_connect() returns 0 without attaching anything
+		 * when the link mode is MLO_AN_FIXED, and a close/reopen cycle
+		 * clears netdev->phydev again.  Keying off the flag left the
+		 * 2.5G port with phy_connected=1 but netdev->phydev==NULL for
+		 * good: ethtool printed only "Link detected: no", the PHY's
+		 * read_status was never polled and the copper never linked.
+		 */
+		if (!dev->phydev) {
 			err = phylink_of_phy_connect(port->phylink,
 						     dev->dev.of_node, 0);
 			if (err) {
@@ -1928,7 +1936,6 @@
 					   __func__, err);
 				return err;
 			}
-			port->phy_connected = true;
 		}
 
 	}
